title crypto/ed25519_to_x25519 — the SECRET half of the birational map, GREEN
prompt take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first; Rye prioritized, Glow on green Rye; send often as its own signed round; stop at custody gates; baton prin recur
think Read REMEMBER, the 1024-round itinerary, the six-season double-seat, and the rye-first crypto decision wave. Season G — Cryptography is the highest-Lindy live spine; the living edge kumara_attestation named the identity arc whole and pointed next at "a Comlink/Vault composition reaching identity through this door."
think The crux there is that a Kumara identity can SIGN (ed25519) but cannot yet RECEIVE an encrypted message — sealed_session.open wants an X25519 secret, and no module derives the identity's X25519 secret from its ed25519 seed. ed25519_to_x25519 mapped only PUBLIC keys. That missing secret half is the one binding move that opens Comlink private messaging (Lindy-first: every DM ever), so it is Round 1; the kumara_sealed composition is Round 2.
think Confirmed the exact derivation against Zig std.crypto: X25519.KeyPair.fromEd25519 computes clamp(SHA-512(seed)[0..32]) — precisely ed25519_sign.expand(seed).a. And crypto/x25519 clamps its scalar internally, so the clamped ed25519 scalar drops straight in.
obs Kept it thin: exposed pub secret_scalar in ed25519_sign (names its own clamped scalar, two clamp postconditions), and eddsa_secret_to_x25519 in ed25519_to_x25519 is a one-line passthrough that NAMES the secret half so the conversion module carries both halves. No new cryptography, no duplicated expand.
obs Parity proven two independent ways across 24 seeds: our x25519_base(secret) equals eddsa_to_x25519(derive_public(seed)) — the secret and public halves name one keypair — and both equal Zig's fromEd25519 secret_key and public_key byte-for-byte. Non-gated; TEST seeds only, deriving from a real seed stays the custody gate (#3/#4).
loom witness=crypto_ed25519_to_x25519_witness result=GREEN seeds=24 parity=zig_fromEd25519+internal
file crypto/ed25519_sign.rye pub secret_scalar exposes the clamped ed25519 secret scalar (the X25519 secret) with clamp postconditions
file crypto/ed25519_to_x25519.rye eddsa_secret_to_x25519 completes the birational map; selftest pins the secret half against Zig fromEd25519
recommend keep-going — Round 2 is crypto/kumara_sealed.rye: seal a message TO a Kumara identity, open it AS the identity, the Comlink private-message door; count guard 55→56, docs+suite sync
